@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-header-is-one-row
Card reading MUST remain full screen. Its fixed header MUST have a 44dp Back
arrow (the reader returns to the gallery; it is not a closing action), a raised
pill with the card's name and a caret occupying the available middle width, and a
44dp Share button; a card with nothing to share leaves that place empty. It MUST NOT
add a second metadata row. Long names may ellipsize to one line in this pill, while
keeping the complete name in text semantics. The pill and controls MUST remain
separate at narrow widths and large font settings. Sheet headers remain plain
titles; this pill belongs to the reader. The card's actions moved to the foot
(`card-reader-foot-holds-its-actions`).
Source: Tavi's attached toolbar reference and one-row requirement, 22 October 2026;
the recorded review of the same day ("this icon here should actually be a back
icon"); Tavi's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026, after his canvas
comment on G08 ("Maybe we can just put a share button there instead").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-shows-the-whole-card
The reader MUST show every part of a card it has, each once, in its own raised
section: the picture (cover, post image or image file) with the title, who made it,
where it is from, when it was saved and how long its page takes to read; the post or
note body, or else the saved summary; the tags; the user's note; and the captured
page text with its reading time. Text sections MUST carry a small muted heading.
The card's type colour MUST wash the top of the reader as a faint fade, as it does
on the card's sheets, and never tint the body. Tags are quiet pills without crosses;
Edit tags reveals a cross on each and Done hides them again, and + Add opens Add
tags.
Source: Tavi's recorded review, 22 October 2026 ("why is there nothing here", "can't
just tint only the bottom sheet", "some tags which look really weird"); Tavi's pick
of F08, whose page is the prototype's 02 raised sections, 28 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] card-reader-opens-its-source
A card with a web link MUST open it from a tap on its picture and from the foot's
Open source pill, which speaks the site's name. Holding the picture MUST open the
card's actions. A card without a link MUST NOT show Open source. A video the server
keeps plays in place instead (`card-reader-plays-videos`), and Open source still
opens its link.
Source: Tavi's recorded review, 22 October 2026 ("especially the preview, I should be
taken to the source"); Tavi's pick of F08, 28 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-foot-holds-its-actions
The reader's foot MUST float Open source, a 52dp pill in the page's ink, and a 52dp
raised round button that opens the card's actions, over a fade into the page, and
the page MUST leave room under its last section so the foot never covers it.
Source: Tavi's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] card-reader-name-grows-into-its-card
Tapping the reader's name MUST grow its pill into a card of the card's details over
a light scrim: its picture beside who made it, where it is from, when it was saved
and its reading time; then Copy link (only for a card with a link), Top of Mind as a
switch, and Spaces naming the card's spaces; then up to three cards opened before
it, each of which opens in its place, and Back to Everything. Copy link and Spaces
hide the card before they act; Top of Mind keeps it open. Tapping the name, the scrim
or system Back MUST shrink it back into the pill before Back closes the reader.
Source: Tavi's pick of F08 in the reader prototype, 28 October 2026.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design] card-reader-shows-the-whole-picture
The reader MUST show a card's picture whole, at its own proportions (kept between a
tall phone screenshot and a wide banner), never cropped to a fixed frame.
Source: Tavi's recorded review, 23 October 2026 ("the image is half cut", "it's not even
like complete").

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;design;motion] card-reader-plays-videos
A video the library server keeps MUST open in the reader as a video player, as Google
Photos does: it starts by itself with sound over its still, a tap on the video pauses
or resumes it, and under it sit play or pause, the time played of the whole, sound on
or off, and a bar to move through it. It MUST pause when the app leaves the screen and
stop when the reader closes, and it MUST only request media from the library server.
Videos on other sites keep their still picture, which opens the source.
Source: Tavi's recorded review, 23 October 2026 ("we should be showing things like kind
of more similar to how Google Photos shows a video", "they open kind of a video player,
which makes far more sense for a video").
